    "https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/7753": {
      "title": "University of Hartford Employment Site | Regional Admissions Counselor - REMOTE POSITION",
      "description": "University of Hartford Employment Site | Regional Admissions Counselor - REMOTE POSITION Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Regional Admissions Counselor - REMOTE POSITION Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Regional Admissions Counselor - REMOTE POSITION FLSA Classification EX Reports to Senior Assistant Director, Admissions Salary Range G Weeks Per Year 52 Work Week 40 hours (minimum) Position Summary Serves as a member of the Admissions Team, managing the assigned recruitment territory to assist in achieving enrollment goals. Provides information about the University of Hartford and the college planning process to prospective students, parents and high school counselors. Manages and execute a comprehensive recruitment schedule in assigned geographic territory. Performs all duties in full support of the University’s mission, understanding that the positive and effective execution of these duties are instrumental to the education of the University’s students. This is a fully remote position and assigned to one of the following areas: Long Island Boston/New England Northern New Jersey/Westchester & Rockland Counties, New York Southern New Jersey/Philadelphia Hiring Range $47,000 Key Responsibilities Key Responsibilities Territory Management & Travel – Independently manages and executes a comprehensive recruitment schedule in assigned geographic territory. Regularly visit high school, high school college fairs, regional college fairs, national college fairs, community-based organization events , transfer college fairs, etc. Outreach & Events – Hosts recruitment and yield events in assigned territory annually. Application Review and Counseling – Advises students/families on admission and next steps. Conducts prospective student appointments and follow-up meetings. Evaluates applications in holistic review process and meet yearly reading goals. Relationship Development & Maintenance – Develops and maintains a strong presence of understanding about the University of Hartford in assigned territory including high-touch service for school counselors, students, and families in assigned region including but not limited to phone calls, emails, texting, virtual meetings, in person visits, and specialized recruitment events. Develops and cultivates strong relationships with school counselors, community-based organizations, independent educational consultants and other influencers in assigned recruitment territory Data & Reporting – Uses Customer Relationship Management , ie. “ CRM ” (Slate) and historical data to set goals, target schools, and report on territory performance and event ROI Relationship Cultivation – Works alongside Development & Alumni Affairs to support alumni events in your assigned territory. Cultivates relationships to develop connections with alumni for support in future recruitment events in your assigned territory. Educates alumni volunteers on the messaging and branding of the University of Hartford. Travels to campus for staff training and on-campus recruitment events as needed. Performs other duties as assigned. Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1200P Working Conditions Normal office situation, requires travel, including overnight stays. Education Bachelor’s Degree Required Physical Effort Typically sitting at a desk or table, moderate lifting or carrying 26-50lbs. Special Skills The ability to work effectively with diverse groups. Valid drivers’ license required Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Quick Link for Internal Postings https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/7752 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Technical School, Certification or Apprenticeship Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree Knowledge of a highly advanced professional discipline. (e.g., Ph.D, M.D., J.D., or equivalent doctoral degree required.) How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation - Staff Statement on Inclusive Excellence and Belonging 200 Bloomfield Avenue\r\nWest Hartford, CT 06117 Back to top Copyright © 2021 University of Hartford To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
